{"version":1,"slug":"Oliiveboardd__GS_Super_Prac__History_07_Establishment_of_British_Rule_and_1857_Revolt_Part_2","path":"Oliiveboardd/GS Super Prac/History_07_Establishment_of_British_Rule_and_1857_Revolt_Part_2.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Oliiveboardd","category":"GS Super Prac","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":10,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following battles is considered the formal beginning of the British Raj in India? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335;&#2367;&#2358; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2346;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">First Carnatic War</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2341;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Battle of Plassey</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Battle of Wandiwash</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Battle of Buxar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The Battle of Plassey, fought in 1757 between the British East India Company and the Nawab of Bengal, marked a pivotal moment in Indian history. This battle effectively established British colonial power in India and is widely considered the beginning of British political dominance in the subcontinent.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>One of the main reasons for the defeat of Nawab Siraj-ud-daulah in the Battle of Plassey was that the forces led by _________, one of his commanders, never fought the battle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2357;&#2366;&#2348; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2351;&#2361; &#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; _________ &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2349;&#2368; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Mahabat Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2348;&#2340; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Jafar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2347;&#2364;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Khalifa</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2326;&#2354;&#2368;&#2347;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Jumla II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2332;&#2369;&#2350;&#2354;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>In the Battle of Plassey, Nawab Siraj-ud-daulah faced defeat primarily because his commander <b>Mir Jafar</b> betrayed him by not fully engaging in the battle. Mir Jafar's collusion with the British, led by Robert Clive, proved decisive in the outcome of the battle, ultimately resulting in Siraj-ud-daulah's defeat and the establishment of British dominance in Bengal.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which military officer led the British forces in the Battle of Chinhat fought in 1857?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>1857 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2330;&#2367;&#2344;&#2361;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2376;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335;&#2367;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Robert Maclagan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2350;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2327;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Henry Lawrence</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2354;&#2377;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">James George Smith</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2375;&#2350;&#2381;&#2360; &#2332;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332; &#2360;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2341;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Charles Ellice</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2360; &#2319;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><b>Battle of Chinhat  -  30 June 1857</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Context</b>: The Battle of Chinhat was a significant early clash during the <b>Indian Rebellion of 1857</b>, fought near <b>Lucknow</b>.</p><p>&#183; <b>British Commander</b>: <b>Sir Henry Lawrence</b>, the Chief Commissioner of Oudh (Awadh), led the British forces.</p><p>&#183; <b>Outcome</b>: The British forces <b>suffered a defeat</b> against the rebel forces, which was a major blow early in the revolt. This forced them to retreat to the <b>Residency in Lucknow</b>, leading to the famous <b>Siege of Lucknow</b>.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The Battle of Buxar was fought between the forces under the command of the British East India Company led by Hector Munro, and the combined armies of ________.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2344;&#2352;&#2379; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335;&#2367;&#2358; &#2312;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; ________ &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Mir jafar, Siraj-ud-Daulah and Mughal Emperor Shah Alam II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2347;&#2364;&#2352;, &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2327;&#2364;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2358;&#2366;&#2361; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Qasim, Mughal Emperor Shah Alam &amp; Shuja-ud-daulah of Awadh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2350;, &#2350;&#2369;&#2327;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2358;&#2366;&#2361; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Jafar, Mughal Emperor Bahadur Shah II, Shuja-ud-Daulah</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2347;&#2364;&#2352;, &#2350;&#2369;&#2327;&#2364;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2348;&#2361;&#2366;&#2342;&#2369;&#2352; &#2358;&#2366;&#2361; II, &#2358;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Siraj-ud-Daulah, Shuja-ud-Daulah, Mughal Emperor Shah Alam II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2358;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2350;&#2369;&#2327;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2358;&#2366;&#2361; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350; II</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The Battle of Buxar resulted in the British establishing their rule by defeating the combined army of Mir Qasim, the Nawab of Bengal, the Nawab of Oudh, and the Mughal Emperor, Shah Alam II.</p><p>Hence, option (b) is correct.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Against whom was the Battle of Plassey (1751) fought by the English Company led by Robert Clive?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; (1751) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Nizam of Awadh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2357;&#2343; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2332;&#2364;&#2366;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Siraj Ud Daulah</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2313;&#2342; &#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Murshid Quli Khan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2368;&#2342; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Shaan Nawab</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2357;&#2366;&#2348;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The Battle of Plassey took place between the British East India Company troops, commanded by Robert Clive, and <b>Siraj-ud-Daulah</b>, the last Nawab of Bengal, along with his French allies.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following led English company in Battle of Plassey(1757)?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; (1757) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Lord Dalhousie</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2337;&#2354;&#2361;&#2380;&#2332;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Captain Hodason</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2376;&#2346;&#2381;&#2335;&#2344; &#2361;&#2377;&#2337;&#2360;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Warren Hastings</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2377;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2361;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Robert Clive</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The Battle of Plassey was fought in north-eastern India on 23 June 1757. Troops of the <b>BritishEastIndia Company, led</b> by <b>Robert Clive</b>, came up against the forces of Siraj-ud-Daulah, the last Nawab of Bengal, and his French allies.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who led the English army in the Battle of Buxar?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Lord Clive</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">William Henry Sleeman</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Hector Munro</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2344;&#2352;&#2379;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Charles Eyrecoot</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2360; &#2310;&#2351;&#2352;&#2325;&#2370;&#2335;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The English army at the Battle of Buxar was led by Major <b>Hector Munro</b>, which took place on October 22, 1764. The battle was a significant conflict during the East India Company's expansion in India and resulted in the victory of the British East India Company forces over a coalition of Indian rulers.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which of the following years did Japan invade India resulting in the Battle of Imphal?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2339; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2311;&#2350;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2354; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1862</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1862</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1944</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1944</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1901</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1901</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1899</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1899</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><b>Battles of Imphal</b> and Kohima</p><p>Fought between 8 March and 18 July 1944, these were the turning point of one of the most gruelling campaigns of the Second World War (1939-45).</p><p>On 7 December 1941, the Japanese attacked the US naval base at Pearl Harbour and later declared war on Britain and the United States.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which year was the Battle of Buxar fought?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1793</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1793</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1777</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1777</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1764</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1764</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1757</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1757</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>&bull; The Battle of Buxar was fought on 22 October 1764 between the British East India Company and the combined forces of:</p><p>o Mir Qasim (Nawab of Bengal)</p><p>o Shuja-ud-Daula (Nawab of Awadh)</p><p>o Mughal Emperor Shah Alam II</p><p>&bull; The battle resulted in a decisive British victory, leading to the Treaty of Allahabad (1765), which gave the Diwani (Revenue collection rights) of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa to the British.</p><p>&bull; This victory strengthened British control over Eastern India, laying the foundation for British colonial rule in India.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who was the Mughal Emperor at the time of Battle of Plassey?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2369;&#2327;&#2364;&#2354; &#2358;&#2366;&#2360;&#2325; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Alamgir II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2354;&#2350;&#2327;&#2368;&#2352; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Siraj-Ud-Daulah</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;-&#2313;&#2342;-&#2342;&#2380;&#2354;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mir Quasim</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Shah Alam II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2366;&#2361; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350; II</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The Battle of Plassey was fought in Palashi (an area of Nadia District, West Bengal), on the banks of the Bhagirathi river near Calcutta on 23rd June 1757. It holds historical significance in Indian history as the British were able to establish their rule in India after this war. The East India Company, led by Robert Clive, defeated the Nawab of Bengal (Siraj-Ud-Daulah) and his French Troop in this battle. It took place at the end of the<b> Mughal Empire's tenure whose charge was with emperor Alamgir-II.</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}